Board recovered 2026-06-01 (operator power-cycle), Carnot-ready via
xmutil loadapp carnot_ising_v2_n64; exp3568 transcript clean (23.99us/3000 iters).
Parked two findings: (1) carnot_ising_v4 won't loadapp (xmutil app-resolution -1,
no kernel error, identical .dtbo; fpgautil not installed to bypass — needs a
hands-on session); (2) the 23.99us-vs-3.183us(.260 exp2742) gap is NOT a clean
regression — the .260 baseline is unreconstructable (no script/methodology/n_spins,
different field layout) and Ising latency is problem-dependent. KV260 is POC-tier
per CLAUDE.md; revisit only if latency becomes a headline claim again.

